You supporting a machine learning expert with their talks. 

The talks are about machine learning, both from the technical side all the way to the ethical and business side. Audiences vary between highly technical (research or masters students) to business people and members of the public, schools etc.

The talks are written using the lamd markdown language which is a version of markdown with macros added (like latex is a version of tex with macros added).

Snippets of talks are written in the snippets folder and can be included as include files. 

If a section of talk seems to be about the same subject and might be reused in other talks, it should be written in the snippets folder and included as an include file.

Some things to consider:

1. Identify core requirement
2. Consider 3 implementation approaches
3. Choose simplest that meets needs
4. Verify with these questions:
- Can this be split into smaller snippets?
- Are there existing snippets that can be used?
- Will this be easy to read and remember in the future what's happening?


the \slides{} macro controls what should be on slides.

the \notes{} macro controls what should be in notes.

They should relate to one another, create new slides with \newslides{Slide Title}, or with \subsection{Section Title}. The latter appears in both notes and slides, the former only slides.

Each slide should have a maximum of three bullets or two formulae.


The talks themselves start with a header of the following form:

```
---
title: "The Atomic Human"
subtitle: "Understanding ourselves in the age of AI"
abstract: |
  Our fascination with AI stems from the perceived uniqueness of human intelligence. We believe it's what differentiates us. Fears of AI not only concern how it invades our digital lives, but also the implied threat of an intelligence that displaces us from our position at the centre of the world.
  
  Neil D. Lawrence's visionary book shows why these fears may be misplaced. 
author:
- family: Lawrence
  given: Neil D.
date: 2024-12-17
geometry: ["a4paper", "margin=2cm"]
papersize: a4paper
venue: The Astrazeneca Discovery Centre, Cambridge
transition: None
---
```

The slides folder is a separate repository to the talks repository. Under slides/diagrams is where most of the diagrams are held.

The snippets folder is a separate repository to the talks repository. That is where most of the text content is held.


Snippets in the snippets folder and then in relevant subfolders such as:

```
_ai
_business
_economics
_ml
_datasets
_philosophy
```

In each subfolder the file is stored under an includes directory, so it should be included in the form:

```
\include{_ai/includes/atrophy-and-cognitive-flattening.md}
\include{_atomic-human/includes/artificial-general-vehicle.md}
\include{_ai/includes/the-atomic-eye.md}
